' A game with somebody on the other side, and a scenario that asks for the
' two places the victory condition wants first: Sana and Bearwoods.
'
' The machine player starts in Sana with nobody to hire, so it walks the two
' days to New Sandez, takes a man on there out of its own pack, walks the two
' days back, and leaves him holding Sana - with its own knife, because a camp
' with no tool in it stores nothing anybody could come and fetch.
'
' The player hires one man, waters both at the Bearwoods spring, leaves him
' holding Bearwoods, and walks on to Sana to arrive after their man has
' settled in.
mapclick 75,303          ' into New Sandez
clickon 248              ' a mercenary, hired with the meat
hire
wait 20
esc
mapclick 61,355          ' sets out; the days on the road pass by themselves (v0.9.1 skips a travelling player's turns)
mapclick 61,355          ' walk in
wait 120                 ' let him close in, so he drinks too
mapclick 500,233         ' the shack with water: everybody within fifty drinks
wait 20
esc
wait 30
join                     ' he stays: Bearwoods is ours
esc
mapclick 150,318         ' sets out; the days on the road pass by themselves (v0.9.1 skips a travelling player's turns)
day                      ' one more after the three on the road: their man settles into Sana on this turn
save                     ' the cut: their camp stands, ours holds Bearwoods
